le":"Data Manager","email":"reedk@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Jessica","last_name":"Bird","role":"Collections Information Manager","email":"birdj@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Diane","last_name":"Pitassy","role":"Acting Collection Manager/Data Manager","email":"pitassyd@si.edu"},{"last_name":"Collection Managers","role":"Collection Managers","email":"NMNH-HerpsCM@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Brian","last_name":"Schmidt","role":"Data Manager","email":"schmidtb@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Darrin","last_name":"Lunde","role":"Collection Manager","email":"lunded@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Orrell","role":"Deputy Director, Research Informatics Program","email":"orrellt@si.edu"},{"last_name":"Informatics and Data Science Center - Digital Stewardship","role":"IPT Administrator","email":"informaticshelp@si.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"32069b11-a9d2-42e2-aa9c-b16350444909","totalCount":9302779,"hitRatio":3.2248428130991827e-7},{"uuid":"4523e216-ee13-4b15-a3f7-a6fd56431604","itemCount":1,"name":"Louisiana State University, Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium - Vascular Plants","description":"Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium at Louisiana State University, Vascular Plant Collection contains 310,000+ specimens. Several regional herbaria are integrated entirely or in part, including NO, LSUS, MCN, NLU, Eglin Air Force Base, and New Orleans Academy of Sciences. Only Tulane University Herbarium (NO) remains a distinct collection.&nbsp;&nbsp;Geographic distribution is global, but strengths are Louisiana and the southeastern USA, southen California, Colorado Rocky Mountains, Yucatan Peninsula, Colombia and Brazil. Families well-represented include Asteraceae, Fabaceae, Cyperaceae, Rubiaceae, and Poaceae. Significant collectors include: Fr. G. Ars&egrave;ne, L. M. Booth,&nbsp;C. A. Brown,&nbsp;I. W. Clokey, R. S. Cocks, D. Demaree,&nbsp;J. A. Ewan,&nbsp;A. Featherman,&nbsp;A. Gray, J. Hale, J. F. Joor, D. D. Keck, E. P. Killip, J. G. Lemmon, Y. E. J. Mexia, F. W. Peirson,&nbsp;N. F. Peterson,&nbsp;J. L. Riddell, and D. Stone,&nbsp;R. D. Thomas, S. C. Tucker, L. E. Urbatsch, I. V&eacute;lez, and E. C. Wurzlow.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/lsu.jpg","url":"http://www.herbarium.lsu.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=210","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/lsu-vascularplants_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Jennifer S. Kluse, Collections Manager","email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Jennifer S. Kluse, Collections Manager","email":"jkluse@lsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":316835,"hitRatio":0.0000031562169583537174},{"uuid":"910eadc8-8131-428c-b28a-91d0e2890f1d","itemCount":1,"name":"Delaware State University, Claude E. Phillips Herbarium","description":"The Claude E. Phillips Herbarium (DOV) at Delaware State University is the only public herbarium on the Delmarva Peninsula (USA) and houses over 200,000 specimens of vascular plants, bryophytes, lichens, fungi, and algae. DOV&rsquo;s collections span more than 200 years of botanical exploration in Delmarva, the neighboring states, and other parts of the U.S. As a regional herbarium, DOV often surprises with its significant historical collection that is worldwide in scope. Ancillary collections of bark; botanical beads; cones, fruits and seeds; dried botanicals; fibers; fossils; potpourri ingredients; wood; and permanent slides augment DOV&rsquo;s holdings.","logo":"https://midatlanticherbaria.org/portal/content/collicon/dov.jpg","url":"https://herbarium.desu.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=334","archivelink":"https://midatlanticherbaria.org/portal/content/dwca/dov_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"chwa@desu.edu"},{"last_name":"Cynthia Hong-Wa","email":"chwa@desu.edu"},{"last_name":"Cynthia Hong-Wa","email":"chwa@desu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"25b6b373-8115-43ee-9fee-a0e1a7262d7f","totalCount":174046,"hitRatio":0.0000057456074830791855},{"uuid":"beab5209-9628-4d4d-851e-2bc9bb1a0105","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Georgia Herbarium","description":"","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/ga_new.jpg","url":"https://www.plantbio.uga.edu/uga-herbarium","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=258","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/ga_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Tanisha","last_name":"Williams","role":"Curator/Director","email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Steven","last_name":"Hughes","role":"Collections Manager","email":"sthughes@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Tanisha","last_name":"Williams","role":"Curator/Director","email":"tanisha.williams1@uga.edu"},{"first_name":"Steven","last_name":"Hughes","role":"Collections Manager","email":"sthughes@uga.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":280846,"hitRatio":0.0000035606702605698496},{"uuid":"d53132e6-7997-4850-8607-4fec5a3f9c3f","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Tennessee Vascular Herbarium","description":"The TENN vascular collection has a strong emphasis on widespread and/or temperate taxa. Even though the collection houses representative specimens of the world's flora, it is unique in having the largest collection of specimens from the state of Tennessee, the historical collections documenting the flora of the Great Smoky Mountains National Park (a World Biosphere Reserve), and the large, general collection from throughout the southern Appalachians. Significant and representative collections are also present from the remainder of the U. S., including Alaska, Central and South America, and Afro-Eurasia. The pteridophyte collection is more cosmopolitan than the rest of the vascular plant collection due, in large part, to the collecting and exchange of A. M. Evans and A. J. Sharp.","logo":"https://swbiodiversity.org/seinet/content/collicon/tenn.png","url":"https://herbarium.utk.edu/vascular/index.php","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=312","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/tenn_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"tennherbarium@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Herbarium","last_name":"Email","email":"tennherbarium@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Dr. Jessica","last_name":"Budke","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"jbudke@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Garrett","last_name":"Billings","role":"Collections Manager","email":"billings@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Herbarium","last_name":"Email","email":"tennherbarium@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Dr. Jessica","last_name":"Budke","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"jbudke@utk.edu"},{"first_name":"Garrett","last_name":"Billings","role":"Collections Manager","email":"billings@utk.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":257797,"hitRatio":0.000003879021090237668},{"uuid":"ddef79ec-043c-4027-9876-c4a298feff6d","itemCount":1,"name":"Florida State University, Robert K. Godfrey Herbarium","description":"The collection contains >220,000 specimens that document the distribution and natural variation of plants and algae worldwide, with a special focus on the 2,400 species of plants found in N FL--one of North America's biodiversity hotspots--and the microalgae of Florida's Gulf and Atlantic coasts.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/fsu.png","url":"http://herbarium.bio.fsu.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/fsu_dwc-a.eml","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/fsu_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"amast@bio.fsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Dr. Austin R. Mast","email":"amast@bio.fsu.edu"},{"last_name":"Dr. Austin R. Mast","email":"amast@bio.fsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":85749,"hitRatio":0.000011661943579516963},{"uuid":"e60301d9-9b40-483f-92de-065769b9d3dd","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Louisiana at Monroe Herbarium, R. Dale Thomas Collection","description":"The R. Dale Thomas Collection - University of Louisiana Monroe (NLU) collection was transferred to the Botanical Research Institute of Texas in 2017. Additionally in 2018-2019, more than 50,000 NLU specimens were transferred to the Shirley C. Tucker Herbarium (LSU) at Lousiana State University. Please contact Tiana Rehman (trehman@brit.org) with any questions regarding the collection.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/nlu.png","url":"http://www.brit.org/research/collections/nlu","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=309","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/brit-nlu_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"trehman@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Tiana","last_name":"Rehman","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"trehman@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Ashley","last_name":"Bales","role":"Collections Manager","email":"abales@fwbg.org"},{"first_name":"Tiana","last_name":"Rehman","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"trehman@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Ashley","last_name":"Bales","role":"Collections Manager","email":"abales@fwbg.org"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":384591,"hitRatio":0.000002600164850451519}],"aggs":{"rs":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":0,"buckets":[{"key":"72d4c3c7-3413-4588-a803-e1a63e0d7